================================================================================
Third-party work this project derives from
================================================================================

This file records source that was taken from other projects and modified. It is
not a dependency list: ordinary declared dependencies (Spring Boot, React,
recharts, PyYAML, ...) are fetched by the build and are not redistributed here.

Two upstreams are recorded, under two different licences. Both permit being
combined into an AGPL-3.0-or-later whole, which is what this project is.
detector/src/worksite_detector/annotate.py carries the same attribution in its
module docstring, because that is the file where both upstreams survive; the two
are meant to be read together and to say the same thing.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Ultralytics YOLO  --  AGPL-3.0-or-later
   https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

AGPL-3.0-or-later, the same licence as this project. (An earlier draft of this
file recorded Ultralytics as Apache-2.0. That was wrong and is corrected here.)

What is used, and where:

  * detector/src/worksite_detector/annotate.py declares `PlanAnnotator`, a
    subclass of `ultralytics.utils.plotting.Annotator`. The base class, its
    19-pair skeleton table and its two colour palettes are used as they ship;
    `box_label`, `text` and `result` are inherited unchanged.

  * `PlanAnnotator.kpts` is a rewrite of `Annotator.kpts`, not a copy of it.
    Every decision the upstream method makes was moved into
    detector/src/worksite_detector/draw_plan.py, which is pure arithmetic
    returning drawing instructions; annotate.py only executes them.

Modifications to the inherited drawing behaviour, stated in annotate.py and
repeated here:

  * `conf_thres` defaults to 0.5, where the base class defaults to 0.25.
  * `radius` defaults to 5, where the base class defaults to `self.lw`.
  * `kpt_line=False` is expressed as an empty `show_skeleton` collection.

Ultralytics YOLO is also the framework the detector runs both models with, and
the framework detector/models/best.pt was trained with: it is a fine-tune of the
`yolov8m.pt` checkpoint (see detector/training/train-args.yaml and
detector/training/training-commands.md). Neither weights file is committed --
.gitignore excludes `*.pt` -- and the detector refuses to start without them,
printing where to obtain them.


