2. yuyoujiang/Exercise-Counter-with-YOLOv8-on-NVIDIA-Jetson  --  Apache-2.0
   https://github.com/yuyoujiang/Exercise-Counter-with-YOLOv8-on-NVIDIA-Jetson
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy is included at
docs/third-party/apache-2.0.txt. This section is the attribution notice that
Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires be retained, and the statement of changes that
section 4(b) requires be carried in the modified files.

What was taken:

  * Its `_Annotator.kpts` contributed the `show_points` / `show_skeleton`
    keypoint and limb filters and the `plot_size_redio` overlay scaling.
  * Its per-gesture table -- keypoint indices plus a maintain/relax angle pair
    per gesture -- was adopted together with that annotator.

Both entered this project as detector/aiModule.py (the annotator at lines
91-143, the gesture table as `sport_list` at the top of the file). That file was
the pre-rewrite program. It is no longer at the tip of the tree: nothing
executed it and it stopped being importable at all on Ultralytics 8.1, so it was
removed before publication rather than left for a newcomer to mistake for live
code.

It is retained, unmodified, in this repository's permanent history, and the line
numbers quoted above and throughout detector/ address that file. Any of these
retrieves it in full from any clone:

    git show 621cfb0:detector/aiModule.py
    git cat-file -p 127729e3
    git log --all --full-history --follow -- detector/aiModule.py

621cfb0 is the last commit that carries the file, and
127729e368402110a4d10bc27c6f96ac4e127f43 is its blob, which resolves however the
surrounding commits are later addressed. It entered the repository as
AIModule/detect/aiModule.py and was renamed, byte-identical, to the path above.

Where the work survives today:

  * The two filters and the size scaling are the `show_points`,
    `show_skeleton` and `size_ratio` parameters of `PlanAnnotator.kpts`, with
    the decisions they drive implemented in draw_plan.py.
  * The gesture table is `_DEFAULT_GESTURES` in
    detector/src/worksite_detector/config.py.

Modifications made by this project (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):

  * The gesture table was reduced from three entries to two, ARMS_UP and
    FRONT_BEND. The third entry, `frontbending`, measures a bend from ear
    keypoints 3 and 4 whose visibility nothing checks; it was deleted rather
    than revived. FRONT_BEND carries the numbers of the table's `bending`
    entry, because that is the entry the adopting code actually read.
  * Each gesture now declares a visibility gate, and the gate must cover every
    keypoint the gesture's angle -- and its posture precondition -- is measured
    from. A configuration that breaks that rule is refused at load time.
  * The left and right angles are measured independently and averaged only over
    the sides that passed their own gate. The adopted code averaged both sides
    unconditionally.
  * Gesture state is keyed by an externally supplied person id instead of a
    person's position in one frame's model output, and the hysteresis latch
    re-arms after each completed repetition instead of latching once.
  * The overlay's "skip this keypoint" test was changed from a modulo against
    the frame size to an exact (0, 0) comparison, and negative coordinates are
    refused for keypoints as well as for limbs.
  * The on-frame repetition-counter banner and the mp4 writer are not
    reproduced.
  * The Kafka publisher, the PPE violation windows, the fall throttle, the
    configuration layer and the entry point are this project's own and have no
    counterpart upstream.

